            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0664" n="588" xml:id="pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5631/222: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">The
                                Hague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-22T11:00:00+01:19">June 22, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 22—5:47 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>46. Legation’s No. 45, June 21, 4 p.m. Explanation of the reaction of the
                    Netherlands authorities to our list of desiderata, I have been told this
                    morning, is this: They fear that if they accept our list in its present form as
                    a basis for negotiation they will <hi rendition="#italic">ipso facto</hi> admit
                    that they are willing to give consideration to the suppression of quotas.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Emmet</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
